description:
FILED s515c (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-11) from the Type-Tiny load probe the s515c brief asked for (`use Type::Tiny; use Types::Standard -all;`).

REPRODUCER (probed vs perl 5.40.3, main code 973bdb1d):

    package Foo::Bar;
    our $X = 5;
    sub f { local our $Avoid = 1; return g() }
    sub g { return defined $Foo::Bar::Avoid ? "A=$Foo::Bar::Avoid" : "undef" }
    package main;
    print Foo::Bar::f(), " ", Foo::Bar::g(), "\n";

perl: `A=1 undef`.  PCL: `read error during load: too many colons in "Bar"` (an SBCL backtrace, nothing runs).

CAUSE: Pl/Parser.pm, the `local our` branch of the local-statement lowering (~line 5040, "Detect 'local our $var'") builds the declaration name as "${pkg}::${var}" with the RAW package name; the sibling `our` branch ~20 lines above it (~line 3449) already routes through `_cl_pkg_designator($pkg)` with the comment "Multi-segment package names (Foo::Bar) must be pipe-quoted".  A second copy that missed the fix (rule 11): the fix is to use the same designator (and the hash init spells `#'equal` where its siblings spell `'equal` -- harmless, but the same copy).  Single-segment packages are unaffected (the name has one `::`).

REACH: Type-Tiny-2.010001 (lib/Type/Tiny.pm:617 and :937 `local our $AvoidCallbacks`), so Type::Tiny does not load at all under PCL; none of the 19 board dists, none of PCL's lib/, the perl-tests uses are all in package main.  The Type-Tiny board batch (the round after s515c) needs it first.

=== DONE (s516b) ===
Pl/Parser.pm: `local our $X` and `our $X` inside a sub now declare the package cell through ONE helper, Parser::_our_cell_decl (prefix from _cl_pkg_designator, the variable through cl_sym; a sigil it has no cell for dies, rule 12).  The reproducer prints `A=1 undef` = perl.  Guard Pl/t/our-local-01.t 30 -> 36 rows (scalar / array / hash in Foo::Bar, a one-segment package, a non-ASCII package, main; each line compared with perl's), inverse-verified on main (all six fail: the file does not load).  Other sites grepped (Pl/*.pm, every "${pkg}::"-shaped interpolation): the rest are perl-name KEYS (Environment tables, prototype lookups, _rewrite_var_uses targets) or already go through cl_pkg (ExprToCL 447/483, Parser 2016); none emits a raw package into a CL symbol.  Gen v2-6084; corpus-diff identical over 111 files (no `our` hash in a sub in the corpus).
TYPE::TINY: Type/Tiny.pm now LOADS.  `use Types::Standard -all` then stopped at #3280 (fixed in the same batch, filler 2) and now stops at #3281 (core B has no shim -- filed, not attempted).
